// 5. Documentation and API Examples
/*
API Documentation Structure:

AppManager Framework
├── Core Interfaces
│   ├── IAppRepository - Abstract app source (marketplace, file system, etc.)
│   ├── IAppInstaller - Abstract installation mechanism (k8s, docker, local, etc.)
│   ├── IAppRuntime - Abstract execution environment
│   └── IConfigurationProvider - Abstract configuration management
├── Concrete Implementations
│   ├── HttpMarketplaceRepository - HTTP-based app marketplace
│   ├── K8sDockerInstaller - Kubernetes/Docker installation
│   ├── K8sDockerRuntime - Kubernetes/Docker runtime
│   └── JsonConfigurationProvider - JSON-based configuration
├── Models & UI
│   ├── ApplicationManager - Main orchestrator
│   ├── AppListModel - QML-compatible app list
│   └── QML Components - Ready-to-use UI components
├── Factory & Plugins
│   ├── AppManagerFactory - Create configured instances
│   └── Plugin System - Load platform-specific implementations
└── Examples & Tests
    ├── Vehicle IVI Example
    ├── Edge Computing Example
    └── Comprehensive Test Suite

Key Benefits of This Architecture:

1. ABSTRACTION: Clean interfaces separate concerns
2. PLUGGABILITY: Easy to swap implementations
3. TESTABILITY: Mock implementations for testing
4. REUSABILITY: Framework works across different domains
5. MAINTAINABILITY: Clear separation of responsibilities
6. EXTENSIBILITY: Plugin system for custom implementations
7. CONFIGURABILITY: JSON-based configuration
8. QML INTEGRATION: Native Qt/QML support

Migration Path:
1. Replace existing tightly-coupled code with framework interfaces
2. Configure implementations via JSON instead of hard-coded values
3. Use provided QML components or extend them
4. Implement custom plugins for specific requirements
5. Test with provided mock implementations
*/